{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.math.*;\nimport java.util.regex.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    static Scanner input = new Scanner(new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in)));\n    static FastReader fastInput = new FastReader();\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        int n = fastInput.nextInt();\n        if (n > 20) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            int[][] points = new int[n][5];\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                    points[i][j] = fastInput.nextInt();\n                }\n            }\n            List<Integer> validIndices = new ArrayList<>();\n            outer:\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                    if (i == j) continue;\n                    for (int k = j + 1; k < n; k++) {\n                        if (k == i) continue;\n                        if (computeAngle(points[i], points[j], points[k]) < 90.0) {\n                            continue outer;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                validIndices.add(i + 1);\n            }\n            System.out.println(validIndices.size());\n            for (int idx : validIndices) {\n                System.out.println(idx);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static double computeAngle(int[] origin, int[] a, int[] b) {\n        double dot = 0.0, lenA = 0.0, lenB = 0.0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < origin.length; i++) {\n            int da = a[i] - origin[i];\n            int db = b[i] - origin[i];\n            dot += da * db;\n            lenA += da * da;\n            lenB += db * db;\n        }\n        return Math.toDegrees(Math.acos(dot / Math.sqrt(lenA * lenB)));\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        private final int BUFFER_SIZE = 1 << 16;\n        private DataInputStream dis;\n        private byte[] buffer;\n        private int bufferPtr, bytesRead;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            dis = new DataInputStream(System.in);\n            buffer = new byte[BUFFER_SIZE];\n            bufferPtr = bytesRead = 0;\n        }\n\n        private void fillBuffer() throws IOException {\n            bytesRead = dis.read(buffer, bufferPtr = 0, BUFFER_SIZE);\n            if (bytesRead == -1) buffer[0] = -1;\n        }\n\n        private byte read() throws IOException {\n            if (bufferPtr == bytesRead) fillBuffer();\n            return buffer[bufferPtr++];\n        }\n\n        public int nextInt() throws IOException {\n            int c, num = 0;\n            while ((c = read()) <= ' ');\n            boolean neg = c == '-';\n            if (neg) c = read();\n            do { num = num * 10 + c - '0'; } while ((c = read()) >= '0' && c <= '9');\n            return neg ? -num : num;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstdio>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass FastReader {\nprivate:\n    static const int BUFFER_SIZE = 1 << 16;\n    FILE* file;\n    char buffer[BUFFER_SIZE];\n    int bufferPtr, bufferLen;\n\npublic:\n    FastReader() : file(stdin), bufferPtr(0), bufferLen(0) {}\n\nprivate:\n    void fillBuffer() {\n        bufferLen = fread(buffer, 1, BUFFER_SIZE, file);\n        bufferPtr = 0;\n    }\n\n    char read() {\n        if (bufferPtr == bufferLen) {\n            fillBuffer();\n        }\n        return buffer[bufferPtr++];\n    }\n\npublic:\n    int nextInt() {\n        int c = read();\n        while (c <= ' ') {\n            c = read();\n        }\n        bool neg = false;\n        if (c == '-') {\n            neg = true;\n            c = read();\n        }\n        int num = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            num = num * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = read();\n        }\n        return neg ? -num : num;\n    }\n};\n\ndouble computeAngle(const vector<int>& origin, const vector<int>& a, const vector<int>& b) {\n    double dot = 0.0, lenA = 0.0, lenB = 0.0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < origin.size(); i++) {\n        int da = a[i] - origin[i];\n        int db = b[i] - origin[i];\n        dot += da * db;\n        lenA += da * da;\n        lenB += db * db;\n    }\n    return acos(dot / sqrt(lenA * lenB)) * 180.0 / M_PI;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    FastReader fr;\n    int n = fr.nextInt();\n    \n    if (n > 20) {\n        printf(\"0\\n\");\n    } else {\n        vector<vector<int>> points(n, vector<int>(5));\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                points[i][j] = fr.nextInt();\n            }\n        }\n        \n        vector<int> validIndices;\n        outer:\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                if (i == j) continue;\n                for (int k = j + 1; k < n; k++) {\n                    if (k == i) continue;\n                    if (computeAngle(points[i], points[j], points[k]) < 90.0) {\n                        continue outer;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            validIndices.push_back(i + 1);\n        }\n        \n        printf(\"%d\\n\", (int)validIndices.size());\n        for (int idx : validIndices) {\n            printf(\"%d\\n\", idx);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012170527770649642, -1.0013530300057027e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00011789103882620111, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.006777428206988e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -7.510157047363464e-06, -0.0011081513948738575, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.3854863431770355e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -0.0002797450579237193, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.002806655131280422, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -0.3260897994041443, -0.2811519205570221, -0.22547124326229095, -6.318072337307967e-06, -2.50339189733495e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.016724614426493645, -0.00010692501382436603, -7.629365427419543e-06, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -0.03373509645462036, 0.0, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -0.20143048465251923, -5.3165931603871286e-05, -5.602820692729438e-06, -2.038458114839159e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -7.152555099310121e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.010697519406676292, -0.014163566753268242, -0.06981450319290161, -8.940656698541716e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0004129749140702188, -3.635817120084539e-05, -5.245195097813848e-06, -3.576272320060525e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -6.437280717364047e-06, -6.794698856538162e-05, -7.068861305015162e-05, -0.001209600013680756, -0.0001892864383989945, -0.01251098420470953, -0.1317605972290039, -0.003932838328182697, -0.026301143690943718, -0.0015291199088096619, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.4238757002167404e-05, -4.6